breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 06 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  with 3 localizing wires  It is inked black entirely  and overinked yellow in the anterior half of the specimen  It is sectioned to reveal an area with a yellow punctate appearance  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  located 0 1cm from the posterior closest margin  A section including the closest margin is submitted in A  rest of the punctate area in B E  tissue away from the area in F G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are six additional separate specimens  Labeled  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  lymph nodes are dissected and entirely submitted in cassettes H K  Labeled  superficial medial margin   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fibroadipose t