re developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 28     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     THE REST OF THE AXILLARY TISSUE HAS BEEN EXAMINED  NINE ADDITIONAL LYMPH NODES ARE PRESENT  VARYING IN SIZE FROM  0 1 CM  TO REMOVED_DATE CM  NO EVIDENCE OF FIBROSED FORMER NODES PRESENT  REMOVED_DATE NODES CONTAINS A SINGLE FOCUS OF METASTATIC CARCINOMA MEASURING  0 1 CM   WITH EVIDENCE OF SLIGHT EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  THE INVOLVED LYMPH NODE IS REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE CM  IN SIZE  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 09 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x x 4 0cm mastectomy specimen with an axillary tail  Short stitch demarcates the superior portion of the specimen and a long stitch demarcates the axillary tail  A skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm with a central  1 0cm in length retraction  is also present  Approximately 2 5cm lateral to the skin ellipse  in the same horizontal plane  is an irregular shaped region of fibrous tissue  with a central area that has an increased firmness and grittiness  compared to its surrounding tissue  This area measures approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  and is approximately greater than 2 0cm from the posterior  closest  margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma has numerous ill defined fibrous areas throughout  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  SECTION CODE  A D  nodular area with increased firmness  E  closest  posterior  margin  F  representative section of fibrous tissue surrounding central firm area  G  fibrous tissue in the inferior anterior medial portion of the specimen  approximately 4 0cm from skin ellipse  H  fibrous tissue in the mid lateral portion of the specimen  greater than 2 0cm from the posterior margin  I M  lymph nodes with the largest lymph nodes  bivalved and submitted as cassette I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and count 27  sentinel node  blue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of fatty tissue  with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm lymph node  Lymph node is submitted in entirety as cassette N  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  GRAY OR 40 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  David Bent Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY CONTENTS PART B  LYMPH NODE  SENTINEL NODE  , Unifocal.
