ared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Rosemary Tambouret MD Signed On  06 MAY 04 at 16 22     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block B   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Rosemary Tambouret MD Signed On  07 MAY 04 at 17 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 7cm tan yellow fibrofatty tissue with stitch marking the nipple orientation  The area at the stitch is inked black  the remainder is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow  finely lobulated cut surface with focal hemorrhagic area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  This area comes closest to with in 0 4cm of the blue inked margin  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast superior hemisphere  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan yellow hemorrhagic soft tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes I L  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  inferior hemisphere left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm tan yellow focally h