ing assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 10     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrofatty tissue fragment  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm ill defined stellate and firm mass which comes to 0 2cm to the closest resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable with focal white fibrotic areas  The stellate mass is submitted in cassettes A and B  The remaining is submitted in toto in cassette C F  Gross Description by  QUN DONG  MD Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS STELLATE AREA  0 7 X REMOVED_DATE CM  FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  QUN DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Peggy Lynn Ueda  M D  PART   B