Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 53 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  FORMING A DOMINANT REMOVED_DATE CM MASS WITH SEVERAL SMALLER FOCI EXTENDING TO THE CAUTERIZED ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  NO METASTATIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA IS IDENTIFIED IN 14 OUT OF 14 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  SEPARATELY RECEIVED SPECIMEN  AXILLA  RIGHT   EXCISION  NO METASTATIC LOBULAR CARCONOMA IS IDENTIFIED IN 1 OUT OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 19 07 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 10 13 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast and axillary   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm skin ellipse containing a nipple and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The posterior deep resection margin is inked black  the superior anterior surface is inked blue  and the inferior anterior surface is inked green  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm stellate shaped rubbery mass with ill defined border  containing a 1 0cm diameter biopsy cavity  The mass extends to within 0 4cm from the deep resection margin  A second focus of scar is located approximately 1 5cm superior to the main biopsy cavity and about 1 0cm from the anterior  and 1 0cm from the posterior resection margin  The rest of the specimen consists of yellow  focally white breast parenchyma with focal cystic area up to 0 2cm in diameter  Dissection of the axillary tail reveals multliple lymph nodes up to 2 0cm in diameter  Section Code  A  mass at the closest margin  deep  B  second scar superior to the first biopsy cavity C D  and E  representative section of the mass around the first biopsy cavity F  tissue around the second  superio r scar N G  1 0cm diameter firm area at the anterior inferior margin  9 0cm inferior from the center of the first biopsy cavity  Q H  breast parenchyma with focal cysts I L  axillary lymph nodes  O P  breast parenchyma with dilated ducts containing white to yellow soft contents  Received within the same container within a specimen cup  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number with no further specification  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan soft tissue fragment  submitted entirely in M  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  AND AXILLARY TAIL PART B  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Multifocal_(multiple_within_same_quadrant).
