Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA  0 9CM  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN 0 2CM OF AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The invasive mammary carcinoma has predominant features of invasive lobular carcinoma  Definite lobular carcinoma in situ is not seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  SCANT  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 17 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with 