Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 19 06 CLINICAL DATA  Status post incisional biopsy which revealed infiltrating ductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY    INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  COMEDO TYPE   MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED    BIOPSY CAVITY WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is predominantly infiltrating carcinoma  The examined resection margins are negative for tumor  however  tumor does approach within 1mm of the deep surgical resection margin  One of twenty eight lymph nodes examined is positive for tumor  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 15                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  The modified radical mastectomy specimen consists of a left breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  an overlying skin ellipse REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm  axillary tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of skeletal muscle  1 5cm inferior and lateral to the nipple is a 2 4cm linear recent healing incision  Beneath this  a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm stellate  hard  white mass extends 0 3cm from the deep margin  It is surrounded by indurated  hemorrhagic breast  The remaining parenchyma is firm and white and contains ill defined tumor  The nipple is unremarkable  The axillary nodes are as large as 0 6cm in diameter and firm and tan white  Section Code A E   nodes from axillary tissue F   lesion with closest deep margin G   biopsy cavity and lesion H K   representative sections of the lesion L   additional lesion distant from the main mass Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS      