mas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 51 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm portion of breast tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 9cm firm  white  irregular region  with infiltrating borders grossly abutting and inked resection margin  The lesion is too small to freeze  The lesion is submitted in its entirety in cassettes A B  Representative sections of the additional  unremarkable parenchyma are submitted in cassettes C J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm focally cauterized portion of white pink  firm breast tissue  which is inked  serially sectioned  and submitted in its entirety in cassette K  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of breast tissue with a suture on one aspect designating the deep margin  The deep margin is inked black  the opposite margin blue  Sectioning reveals predominantly unremarkable adipose tissue  with a small amount of white  fibrous parenchyma  Specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety in cassettes L O  Also received in the same container is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular portion of focally cauterized adipose tissue  There is a suture on one aspect designating the deep margin  The deep margin is inked black  the opposite aspect is inked blue  Specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly firm  white parenchyma  with a small amount of unremarkable adipose tissue  The firmer regions are submitted in their entirety in cassettes P U  Note that 90  of the specimen has been submitted  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  ABUTTING AN INKED MARGIN  LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  SPECIMEN  1 PART B  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  SPECIMEN  2 PART C  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  SPECIMEN  3   report_end  , Unifocal.
