 antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 37     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 neu AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  RIGHT   Less than 5   of the tumor cells stain for HER 2 neu  Favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 06 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE lumpectomy specimen with localizing wire in place  A roentgenogram accompanies the specimen  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular stellate mass which extends to multiple inked margins  A representative section is frozen as FX 1  now A with the remainder in B H  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm lumpectomy specimen  which is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined  pale tan mass extending to multiple resection margins  it is submitted entirely in I L  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKH