ing breast parenchyma contains several ill defined fibrotic areas  the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  located in the lower inner quadrant  extending to within 1 5cm of the closest deep margin and 2 0cm of the closest inferomedial soft tissue margin  In addition  a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrotic biopsy cavity surrounded by bright yellow breast parenchyma is identified subjacent to the skin scar  located 3cm from the deep margin and 8cm from the superior margin  The attached axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple  tan  ovoid  soft lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm  Section code  A  nipple B  skin with scar and underlying biopsy cavity C D firm area with closest deep resection margin E J firm area  representative sections K M fibrotic area  representative sections N R lymph nodes Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Andrew Louis Warshaw  M D  Vikram S Kashyap  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    AXILLA  LEFT  , Unifocal.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 35 CLINICAL DATA  1 5cm invasive carcinoma by core biopsy  Previous history of invasive carcinoma  left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODE  INTRAMAMMARY   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastatic focus consists of just a few cells confined to the lymph node  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   NONSENTINEL    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 45                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lump  is a 4 x 4 x 1 5cm breast specimen that is inked black laterally  red on its deep resection margin  blue superiorly  green inferiorly  It is sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm mass with an irregular border that is 0 3cm from the closest margin  the deep margin   A portion is saved for Dr  Dennis Sgroi  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A through L  with the nodule in cassettes D through J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan blue lymph node with a small amount of associated adipose tissue  The lymph node is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axillary node  non sentinel  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan pink node with a small amount of associated adipose tissue  The lymph node is bisected and submitted in its entirety in cassette N  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPOR