Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 30 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE II  100   DISPLAYING ENDOCRINE CHARACTERISTICS  POSSIBLY INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  In situ carcinoma is not identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 11 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 56 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm fibrofatty tissue fragment  The tissue was inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm white to gray mass abutting an inked margin  Representative sections were frozen as frozen section  1  Representative sections of the remaining tissue are submitted  Section Code  A  closest margins  B E  representative sections of the mass  F  representative section of unremarkable breast  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA    INFILTRATING LOBULAR  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Peter Hedberg  M D  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unifocal.
