er than  2 0 or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for  chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis   The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of  Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID        Addendum  2 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH  23   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 45 45PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART A  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel    Excision  PART B  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  PART C  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  PART D  Skin  Right Mastectomy Flap   Excision  PART E  Skin  Left Mastectomy Flap   Excision  PART F  Cryostat Frozen Section  slide only        report_end  , Unifocal.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 MAY 01 ACCESSIONED ON  10 MAY 01 at 12 36 CLINICAL DATA  Excision of right breast mass    fibroadenoma    malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  HETEROLOGOUS METAPLASTIC TYPE  CHONDROMYXOID MATRIX PRODUCING   GRADE 3 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  PARTLY NECROTIC  LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM INKED MARGINS  See note  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  A minor high grade in situ component is contained within the mass  Tumor comprises most of the specimen  No definite lymphatic or blood vessel invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  14 MAY 01 at 15 08                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block D   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 9x 1 5cm portion of yellow white fibroadipose tissue which is black inked and