 positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  A  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibronodular fibrous tissue with localizing wire  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a stellate firm white lesion with central hemorrhagic focus measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm extending to the inked margin  Specimen is submitted in cassettes A through F  nodule in A   C  representative sections in cassettes D  E  and F  Representative section of nodule frozen and saved  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  B  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fatty fibrous tissue with localizing wire  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm firm  white nodule   1  approximately 1cm from inked margin  and a separate irregular white lesion   2  measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm at the margin  Nodule in cassette G  second irregular lesion  2 in cassettes H and I  Representative sections in J through N  Representative section of rounded nodule  1 saved frozen  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST SPECIMEN A   SMALL CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST SPECIMEN B   SMALL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koern