Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 AUG 97 ACCESSIONED ON  19 AUG 97 at 17 22 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive carcinoma on recent core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  90    REMOVED_DATE CM  GREATEST GROSS DIMENSION OF A STELLATE TUMOR   GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST  DEEP  MARGIN  SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10    LOW GRADE  SOLID TYPE  ASSOCIATED WITH THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  MICROCALCIFICATIONS WITHIN BENIGN BREAST TISSUE  NOTE  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT  DEEP INFERIOR MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 14 OR 14 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  21 AUG 97 at 21 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this 