eft breast stitch at 6 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm left breast simple mastectomy specimen  which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 16 0cm grossly unremarkable  wrinkled white skin  which has a 1 5cm in diameter grossly unremarkable nipple which extends to within 6 3cm of the nearest skin margin  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating 6 o clock  The posterior surface is inked black  The anterior surface is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow  lobulated fatty cut surface with an abundant amount of dense gray white fibrous tissue and multiple intact cysts which contain a tan to brown fluid  The cysts range in size from 0 2cm to 1 8cm in greatest dimension  Also identified within the upper outer quadrant of the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm irregular cystic cavity which contains some gritty gray white material  which may represent the previous biopsy site  The possible biopsy site extends to within 3 0cm of the nearest posterior margin  and 3 5cm of the anterior margin  No other discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire possible biopsy cavity to the overlying nearest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from possible biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 8cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a black stitch designating the 12 o clock position  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 16 0cm tan pink skin ellipse with an eccentric 3 5cm areola  Centrally within the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm unremarkable tan pink nipple which comes to 6 5cm of the superior skin margin  No apparent scars or other gross abnormalities are identified  The anterior margin is inked blue  the posterior black  and is serially s